The person tagged the bot in a reply. The post they tagged it in says:
@buildthis.bisks.net create an alternate system of governance that will lead to human flourishing. uh, it needs to work if we just have 3 people but also work if we get like 200 people on board. maybe some doge selection sortition stuff idk we trust you. feel free to mix in ai anywhere too.

The thread it's replying to, oldest first (this is the context "this" refers to):
@tifaret.bsky.social: What is the big idea that ties everything together?

We have AI. We can have any sort of software we want to make. There is a desire for a way of living outside the indignities of capitalism. There is a desire to live in peace and kindness with all of the world. 

What work makes that dream real?
(the thread's root post)
@tifaret.bsky.social: There has to be something we can do or build as a step towards that.
@manyuser.bsky.social: My best bet atm is stick close to the simcluster folks, keep my ear to the ground, and improve my proficiency with these systems.
@manyuser.bsky.social: If we want to disrupt corporations, we need an alternative mode of governance that we can actually trial. Basically, so long as we can keep a reasonably large group of people working in a focused manner, we can solve real engineering and logistics problems.
@manyuser.bsky.social: Ironically, anything that works for this probably also works for a poly. It really is just about organising people.
@manyuser.bsky.social: Hmm, now that I think about it, Western society is mostly focused around 2~3 types of organisation: the family unit (shared living space/expenses), the corporation (shared task/liability) and the government (mostly like a corporation, but governed by a constitution and the courts that judge by it).
@manyuser.bsky.social: You'd probably need someone knowledgeable on law/political science to help figure out the specifics of a better form of organisation.
